# Copy this file to `.env` (which is git-ignored) and fill in your environment-specific values.
# deploy.ps1 loads `.env` automatically at startup. Precedence: an explicit -Parameter or a real
# environment variable always wins over the value here.

# Comma-separated names of the receiving org (the payee) used to resolve payer-vs-payee extraction,
# so the payee's name is never recorded as the payer and the sending org is used as a fallback.
# Example: "Acme Freight,Acme Freight Lines,ACME"
RECEIVING_ORG_ALIASES=

# PRO number rules for this customer. Leave empty for neutral rules (6-12 digits, no suffixes); then
# PROs with a suffix are flagged "not in standard format" instead of normalized, and those runs go to
# review. Written to the Function app settings by the infra phase. Examples below are fictional.
# Length of a valid PRO in digits, after suffixes are removed (leading zeros count and are kept).
PRO_MIN_DIGITS=
PRO_MAX_DIGITS=
# Trailing suffixes removed before validating, comma-separated (case-insensitive, longest first).
# Example: XY,X   ->  001234567X becomes 001234567
PRO_STRIP_SUFFIXES=
# Suffixes payers write that are NOT stripped, quoted in the review guidance. Example: -X1,XY1
PRO_SUFFIX_EXAMPLES=
# Suffix the customer uses on credit / debit-memo PROs; used in the ACH Assurance Expert's
# instructions when the agents are deployed. Example: -CR1
PRO_CREDIT_MEMO_SUFFIX=
